@startuml video-source-flow
title R12 video input — frame-to-track flow (M1)

|User / FPT-Mentor|
start
:Supply ego-POV clip matching the A-B-C scenario;
:B visible and occluding the lane ahead, C never in frame;

|Build (CI / developer)|
:Preflight the clip with ffprobe against the agreed spec;
if (container/codec/resolution/fps/duration within spec?) then (no)
  :Reject the clip, report the failing attribute;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:COPY media/ into the ADA ECU image at /app/media/;

|ADA ECU detector subprocess|
:Read VIDEO_CLIP_PATH and DETECTOR_FRAME_STRIDE from env;
:Open the clip with OpenCV VideoCapture;
repeat
  :Read next frame;
  if (frame index modulo stride equals 0?) then (yes)
    :Run YOLO11n ONNX on the letterboxed frame;
    :Estimate distance for each vehicle detection;
    :Emit one R3 TrackedObject JSONL line with source own_sensor;
  else (no)
  endif
repeat while (frames remaining?) is (yes)
->no;

|ADA ECU core|
:Ingest R3 JSONL from the subprocess stdout;
:Admit own-sensor tracks through the R13 state machine;
:Compose the scene with relayed C and emit R4 warnings;
:Assert zero detections labeled C over the whole run;
stop

legend right
  <b>Legend — R-numbers are requirement IDs from the report §2, not a message namespace.</b>
  <b>R1–R6</b> are //contract// requirements (deliverable = a schema or a topology); <b>R7–R19</b> are
  //behavioural// requirements (deliverable = running code). "An R3 object" names the artifact R3 defines.
  ====
  |= ID |= Kind |= Meaning on this flow |
  | R3 | contract | <b>TrackedObject</b> schema — the JSONL line the detector emits per detection |
  | R4 | contract | ADA → IVI warning message composed by the core |
  | R12 | behaviour | object detection from video — the detector-subprocess lane |
  | R13 | behaviour | admission state machine: `not_tracked → tentative → tracked` for own-sensor objects |
  ====
  <b>ego / B / C.</b> ego = vehicle A, the warned car · B = the visible occluder ahead, the only vehicle
  A's own camera should ever detect · C = the occluded car, known to A only through the V2X relay.
  <b>`source`.</b> `own_sensor` = seen by A's camera · `v2x_relayed` = received over V2X — never mixed,
  which is what the zero-C assertion checks.
endlegend

@enduml
